            "verdict": "suspicious",
            "normalizedStatus": "suspicious",
            "analysis": "Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: web-slides\nVersion: 2.0.2\n\nThe skill bundle is a functional HTML slide generator, but it is classified as suspicious due to the inclusion of scripts like `chrome-utils.mjs` and `render-preview.mjs` that use `execFileSync` to launch a local headless Chrome process. This creates a vulnerability where an AI agent could be coerced via prompt injection to render sensitive local files into images (LFI) by manipulating the input file paths. While this functionality is plausibly needed for the stated purpose of creating slide previews, the execution of external binaries with agent-controlled arguments represents a high-risk capability that lacks explicit sanitization.",
