            "guidance": "This package is coherent with being a local HTML slide generator. Before running: 1) If you are cautious, inspect the repository locally (scripts use execFileSync to run node and optionally a local Chrome binary). 2) The generator reads bundled theme/reference files and writes outputs under dist/ — run it in a sandbox or an isolated directory if you don't want files mixed into your system. 3) If you don't want headless Chrome invoked, avoid running render-preview/render-preview-related scripts or unset CHROME_BIN; generate the HTML only via generate-slide-html.mjs. 4) There are no network calls, no required API keys, and no hidden endpoints — but as with any third-party code, run it in a controlled environment and review outputs before sharing publicly.",
